From 4b069766eefe1bdd388878d18ee82dd3b25a780a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:39:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(serve): always-on dashboard binds only after its boot
 prewarms finish (bounded) [daveey]

Every hub core update retires the always-on `serve` and systemd starts a new
one. The new process bound its port at once, with the kanban board, session
annotation and project-tree prewarms still running on daemon threads. Desktop
(polling the dead port, failing fast) attached on the first answer and fired
its whole reconnect burst into cold caches: ~60 threadpool threads shared the
GIL with the prewarms, the board prewarm took 39 s instead of ~0.5-4 s
(`kanban board prewarm finished board=default elapsed_s=39.274`, 16:20:12Z
2026-11-12), and /api/plugins/kanban/board plus session reads hit Desktop's
6 s / 30 s deadlines on every core update (t_01a1d0971db77eb3).

uvicorn runs lifespan startup before it binds, so the always-on backend now
waits (asyncio.to_thread, 6 s budget) for the prewarm threads at the end of
`standalone_lifespan`. Desktop's always-on attach treats the closed port as a
supervisor restart and keeps failing fast for up to 20 s
(ALWAYS_ON_RESTART_WAIT_MS), then attaches to a warm backend. Past the budget
it binds anyway (today's behaviour). Desktop-owned `serve --isolated` backends
do not wait (their 10 s ready probe, GH-73083).

The two prewarm starters now remember their boot thread (`boot_thread()`).
